name eoldef
category Package
revision 76050
shortdesc Define commands which absorb the whole source line as arguments
longdesc This macro allows you to define commands that take the entire
longdesc source line as arguments. Usage: \eoldef <control sequence>
longdesc <parameter text> { <replacement text>} defines a control
longdesc sequence that is delimited by the end-of-line in addition to
longdesc the specified parameter text. For instance, \eoldef\test#1:#2{}
longdesc and \test abc:def will give #1 = abc, #2 = def. \eolgdef is the
longdesc \global variant to \eoldef. Like \verb|...|, \eoldef'd commands
longdesc may generally not be used as part of another command's argument
longdesc as it changes catcodes. However, if you must use it in
longdesc environments where catcodes are frozen, you may follow the
longdesc command with a braced argument, eg. \test{#1:#2} using the
longdesc previous example. This package may be used in plain TeX or
longdesc LaTeX by \input{eoldef}.
